/*
 * Football data shared by the Back Room's daily soccer games (Deadline Day, Journeyman, Scout Report,
 * Crossbar, Teamsheet, Back Four, Stat Duel, Top Bins). Plain facts only, written out by hand from
 * public records as they stood in 2025 (careers up to the start of the 2025-26 season). No badges,
 * logos or photos: clubs are drawn as text with two colours picked for this site.
 *
 * Loaded with <script src="../football-data/players.js"></script>; it sets window.FOOTBALL.
 * After editing, run `node e63334287a3deaa3/football-data/check.js` from the repo root: it checks
 * the data and every game's puzzles (careers vs transfers, grid cells, unique answers, aliases...).
 *
 * LEAGUES  code -> name of the country (or league) a club plays in. Monaco counts as France,
 *          Swansea and Cardiff as England, Toronto/Vancouver/Montreal as MLS.
 * NATIONS  code -> [name, continent]. Continent is geographic (Turkey and Georgia: Europe; Australia: Oceania).
 * CLUBS    code -> [name, league code, colour 1, colour 2]
 * P        one row per player:
 *          [name, nation, position GK/DF/MF/FW, birth year, shirt, career, aliases, extra]
 *   shirt   the number he is best known for at his main club (0 = left out because we weren't sure)
 *   career  first-team spells in order, "CODE start-end", separated by ';'. "~" marks a loan.
 *           "2023-" means still there at the start of 2025-26. Reserve/B teams are left out.
 *           A "+" token means the list is NOT complete (minor or uncertain spells left out); such players
 *           are kept out of games that need a full career (Journeyman, Back Four's club groups).
 *   aliases other names people type, separated by '|' (accents never matter; surnames work when unique)
 *   extra   space-separated facts: main:CODE (main club when the longest-spell rule would pick another),
 *           wc:years (in a World Cup-winning squad), bdo:years (Ballon d'Or), caps:n ig:n (men's senior
 *           international caps / goals, only for players who have finished playing for their country),
 *           plg:n (Premier League goals, only for players who have left the Premier League)
 * Anything we weren't sure about is simply left out.
 */
